    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ramat Gan’s name translates to “Garden Height,” a nod to its lush parks and gently rolling hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/ramat-gan-3897"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1968, Ramat Gan opened the world’s largest diamond exchange, solidifying its status in the global trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramat_Gan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Moshe Aviv Tower, Israel’s tallest building, crowns Ramat Gan, while its lower floors will house a chocolate museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
